{"path":"cpp/container/array/back.html","id":"ref-ceafef68ce79c4f0","name":"std::array<T,N>::back","declarations":[{"code":"reference back();","notes":"(since C++11) (constexpr since C++17)","since":"11","until":null},{"code":"const_reference back() const;","notes":"(since C++11) (constexpr since C++14)","since":"11","until":null}],"headers":["array"],"intro":"Returns a reference to the last element in the container.\n\nCalling back on an empty container causes undefined behavior.","sections":[{"title":"Parameters","text":"(none)"},{"title":"Return value","text":"Reference to the last element."},{"title":"Complexity","text":"Constant."},{"title":"Notes","text":"For a non-empty container c, the expression c.back() is equivalent to *std::prev(c.end())."}],"examples":[{"code":"#include <cassert>\n#include <array>\n\nint main() {\n    std::array<char, 4> letters{'a', 'b', 'c', 'd'};\n    assert(letters.back() == 'd');\n}","output":null,"outputKind":"Behavior demonstrated in code","unicodeEscaped":false}],"summary":"Returns a reference to the last element in the container.","source":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/back","introduced":"11","removed":null}
